drm/amd/amdgpu: do not query RAS capability from a VBIOS that is not there

TEST-BED PATCH, not part of the ionic series. On v7.4-rc3 the in-tree amdgpu
oopses while probing the emulated gfx1250 GPU (rocjitsu, no VBIOS image,
MP0 15.0.8): amdgpu_ras_init() -> amdgpu_ras_check_supported() ->
amdgpu_ras_query_ras_capablity_from_vbios() ->
amdgpu_atomfirmware_mem_ecc_supported() -> amdgpu_atom_parse_data_header()
with adev->mode_info.atom_context == NULL.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ras.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ras.c
@@ -3366,6 +3366,9 @@
 /* Query ras capablity via atomfirmware interface */
 static void amdgpu_ras_query_ras_capablity_from_vbios(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 {
+	if (!adev->mode_info.atom_context)
+		return;
+
 	/* mem_ecc cap */
 	if (amdgpu_atomfirmware_mem_ecc_supported(adev)) {
 		dev_info(adev->dev, "MEM ECC is active.\n");
